label: Parcel Request
description: >-
  One parcel to resolve, as it enters the pipeline. The external trigger:
  one request is one run.

  FRICTION (run granularity): this is a lie about blue-ribbon's real unit of
  work. The real ETL is `batch.ts` over a Blue Ribbon corridor -- 17,839
  parcels across 5 counties in one invocation, ending in ONE parquet file.
  Modelling one parcel as one run makes the parquet write homeless, because
  it is a fold across every run and "nothing joins across correlation ids by
  design". See friction #4 in the report. I picked per-parcel because it is
  the only granularity that actually runs.
fields:
  pin:
    # The PIN is public record, but it is the join key into BS&A assessor
    # records (owner name, mailing address, valuation). It is not pii; it is
    # the capability to obtain pii. weir has one axis here and I want two.
    # See friction #7.
    classification: linkable
    type: utf8
    label: PIN
    description: >-
      The county parcel identification number, canonical dash-separated form.
      Segment count and width are a county convention, not a fixed shape --
      "10-003-013-20" (Osceola) and "062-026-300-020-00" (Iosco) are both valid.
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 8
      maxLength: 40
  county:
    type: utf8
    label: County
    description: Which Michigan county's adapter resolves this PIN
    nullable: false
    enumValues:
      - Osceola
      - Manistee
      - Roscommon
      - Iosco
      - Otsego
